WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.610
Some years ago,

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.000
this little town became famous

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.230
for having five centenarians

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.490
and made it to the cover
of National Geographic

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.452
having five centenarians out
of a couple of thousand people.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.410
Molochio is a blue zone.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.290
These are regions of the world
where people live much longer

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.373
and healthier than the average.

00:01:15.373 --> 00:01:19.270
The oldest person recorded
here was Salvatore Caruso.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:21.580
He's what you'd call a super centenarian,

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.240
having made it to 110.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.240
He passed away in 2015,

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.413
but not before assisting those
in search of eternal youth.

00:01:30.324 --> 00:01:33.560
I think Salvatore has been
an inspiration, right,

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:38.560
to say well, I followed this
person for the last 50 years

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.650
of his life or so.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:43.390
And he made it to 110 healthy.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:45.970
So I've seen 110 healthy.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.390
I've seen it with him, but
it's not gonna be doable

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.680
for the the entire world population.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:51.820
It's gonna be doable, I think,

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:55.593
for the people that listen and
follow all the right moves.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.590
Valter Longo has spent
the past two decades

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:01.470
identifying the optimum foods

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.673
and fasting practices for
living healthier and longer.

00:02:05.754 --> 00:02:09.440
Now he's preparing for his
largest human study to date

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.520
here in a remote Italian
town, famous for centenarians.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.470
This clinical trial that was just funded

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:18.770
by the European Community
is gonna take 500 people

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.600
and it's gonna split them into two.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.590
And it's gonna allow half of them

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.500
to sort of have the the bad modern habits.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.090
Now, they are very different

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:28.820
from those of the centenarians.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.340
So we take half of them
and we let them be,

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:34.650
have this Western-like diet
and we take the other half

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.260
and we bring them back
to the longevity diet.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.290
Longo created the longevity diet

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.940
by combining scientific
research and lab work

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.453
with the study of
centenarians around the world.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.620
Longo will also be testing

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.070
his Fasting Mimicking Diet

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:16.410
which offers the benefits
of prolonged fasting

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.640
without having to actually fast.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.020
Fasting has been done for
thousands of years, of course,

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:25.220
but we now have to move
away again from these ideas,

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.260
words like eating or fasting,

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.010
they both mean very little

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:35.860
and move into exactly what
do we eat and how do we fast?

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.837
So it shouldn't be about
now we're gonna turn

00:03:38.837 --> 00:03:42.760
everybody into a biohacker
and use technology

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.101
and distort everything.

00:03:44.101 --> 00:03:46.950
Instead we should learn from the past

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.293
and unite that with the science.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.910
I plan to discuss with you

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.350
what I believe to be the most profoundly

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.140
transformational concept

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:07.690
and strategy as it pertains
to health and aging.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:10.130
So is this your first meal of the day?

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:12.070
It's now almost six o'clock

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:13.028
It will be. Yeah.

00:04:13.028 --> 00:04:14.170
Because?

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.980
Well, because it's clear
based on thousands of years

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:22.450
of human existence that eating less is...

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:25.190
If it's not starvation, or
malnutrition, it's good for you.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:26.140
Because why?

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:30.700
Yesterday I started this thing
called intermittent fasting

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.240
Which is everybody's doing it.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:38.150
Fasting is such an interesting part

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.390
of the longevity conversation.

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:45.050
We've looked at cultures where
fasting is a practice, right?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.870
Where there's ritual fasting.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:47.790
And asked a question of, well,

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:50.313
why are these people living so long?

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:56.450
So we know that fasting does kick off

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.150
certain biological processes

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:03.100
that seem to also have a
connection to longevity.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.170
What we don't know at this point is

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.610
how long do you have to fast?

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.060
Does it work for everyone?

00:05:08.060 --> 00:05:09.680
Or there are just certain people

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.760
of certain genetics for whom that works?

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.260
So there's still a lot of questions,

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:15.850
but at this point it
definitely does appear

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:20.850
that restricting what you
eat might have some impact

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.310
on how long you live
and how healthy you are.

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:26.960
Intermittent fasting,
time-restricted feeding,

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.150
and calorie restriction are
just some of the popular methods

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.063
being adopted.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.760
And while cutting down on meals

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.920
has long been viewed
as a weight loss hack,

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:37.670
it's increasingly being practiced

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.220
as a measure to delay the aging process

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.883
and stave off chronic
diseases that accompany it.

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:45.810
Studies have shown it has the potential

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:49.150
to protect against a range
of age related diseases,

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:52.853
diabetes, heart disease and
cognitive decline to name a few.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.060
But one hurdle remains,

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.430
very few people want to do it.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.440
Have you done it yourself?

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.918
I've done it myself, yes.

00:06:00.918 --> 00:06:04.680
I've fasted for four days, several times.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.521
And to me, it was very tough. Yeah.

00:06:06.521 --> 00:06:09.880
Longo began his research in the early '90s

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.480
identifying the genes
associated with aging

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:14.173
and how nutrients affect them.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.650
Longo tested different fasting methods

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.880
and their effect on longevity in organisms

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:23.200
ranging from yeast to mice, to humans.

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:26.010
He found that cycles of
fasting and re-feeding

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.350
cause multi-system regeneration,

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.190
enhanced cognitive performance,

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:32.633
and the potential to
prevent and treat disease.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.200
It's hard to imagine something

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:38.250
that will do more to
a person than fasting.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.970
If you look at gene expression.

00:06:39.970 --> 00:06:43.980
So if you look at how the
genes are activated or not.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:45.730
One of the key mechanisms at play

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:48.000
is a process known as autophagy

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.253
which literally means self-eating.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:54.700
During autophagy cells
destroy viruses and bacteria

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.290
and get rid of damaged structures

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.600
in order to regenerate
newer, healthier cells.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:01.420
Damaged cells can speed up aging

00:07:01.420 --> 00:07:03.640
and lead to cancer if
they're not destroyed.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:07.080
So this process is vital
to health and lifespan.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.740
The best known way to
activate autophagy in humans

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.030
is fasting.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:12.583
We started with water only fasting

00:07:12.583 --> 00:07:17.583
and we started with a cancer
trial using water only fasting.

00:07:18.110 --> 00:07:20.800
And we thought, of course,
somebody has cancer.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.520
They're gonna be motivated to do this

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.990
and they're not gonna have
a problem with five days

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:28.870
of water only fasting, but we were wrong.

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.690
So it was the U.S.
government that eventually...

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:33.200
and the National Cancer Institute

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.490
and eventually the National
Institute on Ageing

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:38.160
that funded research for
the Fasting Mimicking Diet.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:41.060
Longo created the Fasting Mimicking Diet

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.950
or FMD, a meal plan

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.311
that's formulated to
stimulate a fasting state

00:07:45.311 --> 00:07:47.470
while providing nutrients and calories

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:49.260
through small amounts of food.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:50.240
The Fasting Mimicking Diet

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.850
is a high fat, low protein,
low sugar, low calorie diet

00:07:54.850 --> 00:07:57.360
and starts with a 1100
kilocalories on day one

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.702
and it drops to about 800 kilocalories

00:07:59.702 --> 00:08:02.010
on day two, three, four, five,

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:05.310
usually between 70% to 90% compliance.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:08.610
So most people don't have a
problem doing this once a month

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:11.160
or so for a number of cycles.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:13.000
The FMDs calorie restriction

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:15.240
mimics the body's physiological response

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.083
to traditional fasting methods.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.400
But it's not as simple as
just restricting calories.

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.020
Longo and his team spent years

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.870
perfecting nutrient combinations

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:25.940
that can be consumed

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.950
without triggering the
body's food sensing pathways.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:31.377
You place a system on a
Fasting Mimicking Diet

00:08:31.377 --> 00:08:33.370
and the system starts to shrink.

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:37.050
And what we are seeing is
that the damaged components

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.570
are being removed first.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:43.240
And then we thought, well, if
this Fasting Mimicking Diet

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.290
preferentially kills damaged components,

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.080
rebellious components,

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.810
is it possible that it'll
go after the cancer cells?

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:52.360
The autoimmune cells? The
insulin resistant cells?

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:54.609
For the past 10 years
we've been focusing on that

00:08:54.609 --> 00:08:58.780
and finding that they do.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.880
While Longo and his team
see promising results

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:03.790
among patients suffering
from a variety of diseases.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:07.760
He stresses the FMD is not
an alternative to drugs.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.170
Instead it works most effectively
in combination with them.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:13.520
And I think that the doctor of the future

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.650
is gonna need to know
lot more about these.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.920
And especially now that
in the United States,

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.920
healthcare costs are approaching
about 20% of the GDP,

00:09:23.184 --> 00:09:25.440
so this is not sustainable.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:30.210
And food obviously is the best way to go.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.230
Having gone through 30 clinical trials,

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:36.240
the FMD is in the process
of getting FDA approval.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:39.768
For cancer now we have
just gone to the FDA

00:09:39.768 --> 00:09:42.390
and filed what's called an IND.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.140
So to make food into a drug, right?

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:49.670
So how can food be now
used for cancer patients?

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.700
Longo has developed a
meal delivery service

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:55.820
called Prolon, which people
can buy the meals for the FMD.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.240
And he recommends speaking
to a medical professional

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.263
before starting.

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.060
He says he donates all his profits

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:03.663
from Prolon to research.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.780
Well, first of all,

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:11.240
I think Valter is wrong, but he and I

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.720
have always disagreed on
pretty much everything.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.610
David Sinclair is another heavyweight

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:19.040
in the field of longevity
and represents the conflict

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:21.763
that still exists within
this scientific community.

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.170
While the pair agree on
the biological mechanisms

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:27.050
at play during a fasting state,

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:29.200
they disagree on which are most important

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.340
and the best way to activate them.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.080
If there's one thing I
would recommend in midlife

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:35.960
to do that could extend
your lifespan, it's fasting.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:38.310
We find, my colleagues and I find that

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:40.730
it's not so much how much
you eat and what you eat

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:42.260
it's when you eat.

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:45.110
And so don't always be fed.

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:47.354
Don't always give into those hunger pains.

00:10:47.354 --> 00:10:51.040
I drink tea and I actually don't eat

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.280
probably till late lunch
or dinner every day

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.960
as a way to get those body
defenses going everyday.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:01.350
On an average day,
Sinclair fast for 22 hours,

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:03.360
eating just one large meal.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:05.290
He encourages long daily fasts

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.250
to instigate a biological
process called hormesis.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:12.360
Hormesis is the adaptive
response of cells and organisms

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:15.003
when the body is put
under moderate stress.

00:11:15.003 --> 00:11:17.590
Short bursts of stress, such as fasting

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.650
stimulate the body's mitochondria,

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:23.223
which convert food and oxygen
into energy for cells to use.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:26.600
The body's mitochondria
play a crucial role

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.300
in supporting major organs,

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:30.723
but its functionality decreases with age.

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:33.590
Hormesis has been found to improve

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.270
the mitochondrial performance,

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.453
therefore improving life and health span.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.250
These processes that we're studying.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:43.640
These basically enhancing
our own innate defenses

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:45.710
against disease, they exist within us

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:48.010
and we don't need
medicines to turn them on.

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:50.320
We can skip a meal.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:52.480
We can become exhausted from running.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:53.670
We can lift weights.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.420
We can eat the right
foods, focus on plants,

00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:57.350
this kind of stuff.

00:11:57.350 --> 00:11:58.750
And we actually know

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:01.900
just like epidemiologists have figured out

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.460
that these are the things you can do

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:06.483
to enhance those defenses.

00:12:07.632 --> 00:12:10.750
While Longo acknowledges
the role of hormesis,

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:14.290
he suggests there may be
downsides to this kind of fasting.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:15.123
For example,

00:12:15.123 --> 00:12:19.350
now we know that if you
fast every day for 16 hours

00:12:19.350 --> 00:12:21.100
and that involves skipping breakfast,

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:24.020
that can actually be negative
for you in the long run.

00:12:24.020 --> 00:12:27.060
And there is association
will reduced lifespan.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:29.680
We also know that if you fast for too long

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.370
your metabolism could slow down,

00:12:31.370 --> 00:12:33.540
which may make it difficult

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:37.170
for you to maintain a lower weight.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.390
While experts in the field

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:42.230
may disagree on specifics,
they're all agreed on one thing,

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:45.440
disinformation around
fasting is a major concern.

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:46.480
It's unfortunate.

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:50.180
99% of what's out there
is complete rubbish.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.560
And so what I'm trying to do as a service

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.990
is to speak to the public and say,

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:58.240
there is this group of scientists

00:12:58.240 --> 00:13:00.249
who are publishing the
world's top journals

00:13:00.249 --> 00:13:03.460
that really are making
progress in this area.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:06.640
And while we don't have
anything to prescribe just yet

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:07.473
it is coming soon.

00:13:07.473 --> 00:13:09.173
And certainly there are things
you can do in your lifestyle,

00:13:09.173 --> 00:13:11.000
with your lifestyle

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.810
that'll get you ready for when those come.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.440
Longo hopes his upcoming trial

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.193
can move the conversation along.

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:22.070
The 18-month study in Molochio
will split 501 participants

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:25.870
aged 30 to 65 into three groups.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:29.140
One will be a control group,
so keep their usual diet.

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:32.400
One keeps their diet and
has three cycles of FMD.

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:36.010
The final will be following
the daily longevity diet.

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:38.304
The longevity diet is more a lifestyle.

00:13:38.304 --> 00:13:42.870
So it's an everyday diet,
and this is mainly vegan

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.620
but not only vegan

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:49.620
because you find also the
fish, especially small fishes.

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:55.750
So avoiding the accumulation
of mercury, for example,

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:57.690
which is neurotoxic.

00:13:57.690 --> 00:14:01.920
And there are also some fasting periods,

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:06.650
for example the overnight
fasting, which is around 12 hours.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:10.330
And this is very important
to improve metabolism

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:13.700
and to connect with the circadian rhythm.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:14.710
All participants

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.770
will be followed by
nutritionists like Cervigni,

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:20.660
who will monitor and
review their biomarkers.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.730
In order to define the best diet,

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:25.560
it is important to put
together a lot of information

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:29.940
both from scientific field,
but also from the population.

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:34.430
So in this way, you can
test the information

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:37.490
that come from science in the feasibility.

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:41.383
So which of the informations
that come from science

00:14:41.383 --> 00:14:44.803
can be applied in everyday life.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:49.380
So I think that as we change our idea

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.540
of what it means to be healthy

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:55.310
and look instead at what are
the the biometric signals

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:58.380
of health, what's your blood
pressure, stuff like that,

00:14:58.380 --> 00:14:59.786
we're gonna see more emphasis

00:14:59.786 --> 00:15:03.750
on getting people to eat
foods that are good for you

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:07.240
and to exercise, than just
asking people to lose weight

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:08.513
so they can be healthier.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:11.550
Huge discoveries have been made

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.440
in the field of longevity and nutrition

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:16.743
over the past two decades,
but it's still early days.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.363
Most research has been
done in cells and animals.

00:15:20.363 --> 00:15:22.670
And while this has provided early clues

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:25.680
to how periods without food
may affect the human body,

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:27.160
it will be the clinical trials

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:28.470
that offer the most insight

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:31.530
into how we can reach 100 healthy.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:35.600
Yesterday for me was the
first time I met centenarian

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:40.033
and I realized what longevity means.

00:15:40.892 --> 00:15:45.892
So living long, but being
healthy and being present,

00:15:46.043 --> 00:15:48.310
be happy with your family.

00:15:48.310 --> 00:15:53.310
And I think if diet can help
reach longevity in this way

00:15:54.860 --> 00:15:56.173
it's really worth it.

